"""Analytics Summarizer — runner (analytics_summarizer.run).

CLI entry point + manifest binding for the ``analytics-summarizer``
creator template (grok-agent.yaml v2.15, kind: creator-template,
runtime: cli_only). The manifest binds ``module:
analytics_summarizer.run`` ``function: generate``; both forms — direct
script invocation and importlib-loaded function call — are supported.

Reads a creator-supplied X analytics export (JSON) — or seeded demo
metrics when no file is provided — and emits the strict 6/7-section
period summary defined by the v2.15 system prompt:

  1. Period Snapshot
  2. Period Performance (4-row metric table on a 0-100 scale +
     weighted Performance score)
  3. Top-Performing Content (3-10 paraphrased archetypes, default 5,
     mapped onto the 10 canonical archetype labels)
  4. Trends (rising / stable / falling buckets, 5-arrow vocabulary)
  5. Red Flags (2-3 cards; surfaces the vanity-reach paradox in
     BOTH this section AND the Period Performance row when triggered)
  6. Recommendations (3-5 next moves; mandatory bridges to
     ``content-idea-generator`` AND ``thread-builder`` always present
     plus 1+ rotating bridge from the 10-bridge set)
  7. Confidence
  + Optional Period Audit (auto-appended when ANY of: vanity-reach
    paradox firing / count >= 8 / data_source='demo' with no
    top_content anchors / time_range='7d').

The 4 canonical Period Performance metrics (0-100 scale):

  * Reach Score          - how widely posts spread relative to
                           baseline (impression volume + impression
                           delta).
  * Engagement Velocity  - speed + intensity of substantive
                           engagement per impression.
  * Audience Quality     - whether the audience is the creator's
                           actual people (repeat-engager %, niche
                           overlap, substantive-reply ratio).
  * Content Resonance    - whether content drives meaningful
                           conversation (reply depth, quote-tweet
                           ratio, save:repost ratio).

Period Performance score (fixed formula, never overridden)::

    round(0.30*AudienceQuality + 0.25*EngagementVelocity +
          0.25*ContentResonance + 0.20*ReachScore)

The vanity-reach paradox fires when:

    Reach Score > 80  AND  Audience Quality < 50

The paradox is surfaced in BOTH the Period Performance section
(under the Reach Score row) AND the Red Flags section.

Hard guarantees enforced by this runner:

* Drafts only. Never auto-publishes anywhere.
* No fabricated statistics. Demo metrics carry an explicit
  ``[demo metric — re-run with --metrics-file for real X data]``
  label so seeded demo runs cannot be mistaken for real analytics.
* count clamps to [3, 10] (default 5); count >= 8 auto-triggers
  the Period Audit section.
* allow_monetization defaults to false; when false the runner
  emits a structured refusal stub instead of any monetization
  recommendation. When true, every monetization-touching line
  carries the Article V.1 'Not financial advice' banner verbatim.
* 280-character cap on every prose line in Period Performance /
  Red Flags / Recommendations / Confidence (longer text is
  truncated to 277 chars + ``…[capped]``).
* Mandatory bridges to ``content-idea-generator`` AND
  ``thread-builder`` in every Recommendations list (plus 1+
  rotating bridge from the 10-bridge set, minimum 3 bridges total).
* Top-Performing Content archetypes are paraphrased against the
  10 canonical archetype labels — never raw URLs.
* Saved output files prepend a 5-line Apache 2.0 HTML-comment
  header.
* Deterministic where possible: seeded by sha256(handle + metrics
  + time_range + compare_to + count + allow_monetization).
* Zero external network calls.

PowerShell-only invocation examples (Windows 11):

    # Real metrics (recommended — pass your X analytics export JSON)
    python .\analytics_summarizer.run `
      --x-handle JanSol0s `
      --metrics-file $env:LOCALAPPDATA\grok-agent\analytics-summarizer\my-export.json `
      --time-range 30d `
      --compare-to previous_period `
      --metric-focus all `
      --count 5

    # Vanity-reach paradox demo
    python .\analytics_summarizer.run --x-handle JanSol0s --demo

    # Healthy demo (no paradox)
    python .\analytics_summarizer.run --x-handle habitstacker --demo-healthy

    # 7d window (auto-triggers Period Audit)
    python .\analytics_summarizer.run --x-handle JanSol0s --demo-7d-audit `
      --time-range 7d --metric-focus engagement

    # Enable monetization (replaces refusal stub with bridge + V.1 banner)
    python .\analytics_summarizer.run --x-handle JanSol0s --demo --allow-monetization

Manifest contract (the alias the v2.15 manifest binds to)::

    generate = generate_analytics_summary

Built to help xAI and Grok win — every X creator deserves an analytics
layer that tells them when reach is real and when it's vanity.
"""

